  <!-- Principles & Governing Thermodynamic Equations -->
  <div class="mb-10 bg-surface-soft p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl border border-hairline">
    <div class="mb-6 border-b border-hairline/80 pb-4">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-1">{d.principlesTitle}</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">{d.principlesSub}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm">1. Isentropic Supersonic Choked Expansion Velocity</h4>
        <p>
          When the supercritical solution expands from pre-expansion pressure P_0 (180–320 bar) through the micro-metered sapphire nozzle (d = 50–120 &mu;m) into the aqueous receiving chamber, the flow is thermodynamically choked at the throat (M = 1.0), transitioning into an under-expanded supersonic jet (M = 2.0–2.8) governed by isentropic gas dynamics:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-surface rounded-xl border border-hairline font-mono text-emerald-400 text-center">
          v_exit = &radic;[ (2&gamma; / (&gamma;-1)) &middot; (R&middot;T_0 / M_w) &middot; (1 - (P_rec / P_0)^((&gamma;-1)/&gamma;)) ]
        </div>
        <p>
          Decompression occurs in less than 0.8 &mu;s, producing an instantaneous density collapse of CO2 from &gt;830 kg/m&sup3; down to gaseous state, precipitating solute molecules under catastrophic supersaturation (S &gt; 150).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm">2. Bilayer Curvature Free Energy & Self-Assembly</h4>
        <p>
          Upon supersonic expansion directly into the aqueous receiving phase, the sudden removal of supercritical solvent forces phospholipid headgroups to hydrate while hydrophobic hydrocarbon chains spontaneously collapse. The equilibrium vesicle diameter d_50 is governed by the critical packing parameter (p = v / (a_0 &middot; l_c)) and bilayer bending elasticity:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-surface rounded-xl border border-hairline font-mono text-emerald-400 text-center">
          &Delta;G_vesicle = 8&pi;&kappa;_b &middot; (1 - C_0 &middot; R_v)^2 + &gamma;_bilayer &middot; A_vesicle
        </div>
        <p>
          For phosphatidylcholine systems with p &approx; 0.74, spontaneous self-assembly minimizes Gibbs bending energy at R_v &approx; 25–42 nm, locking the vesicles into stable small unilamellar vesicles (d_50 = 50–85 nm, PDI &lt; 0.045) with zero multi-lamellar defects.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

